    {
      "id": "dec_7e32051c05b34a5ea4ee937e1c630226",
      "kind": "constraint",
      "summary": "No. The `.claude` directory is **project-level infrastructure** — a single shared directory for hooks, skills, state, and configuration across the whole project. Each plugin lives at `.claude/plugins/<name>/` or `.claude/skills/<name>/` as a package unit. If every plugin created its own `.claude/`, you'd fragment hook registration, state paths, and session tracking across dozens of nested directories with no unified owner. The established pattern is: plugins write state to `P:/.claude/hooks/state/` (the canonical shared location) or to their own subdirectory within the plugin path — never to their own `.claude` folder.",
      "details": "No. The `.claude` directory is **project-level infrastructure** — a single shared directory for hooks, skills, state, and configuration across the whole project. Each plugin lives at `.claude/plugins/<name>/` or `.claude/skills/<name>/` as a package unit. If every plugin created its own `.claude/`, you'd fragment hook registration, state paths, and session tracking across dozens of nested directories with no unified owner. The established pattern is: plugins write state to `P:/.claude/hooks/state/` (the canonical shared location) or to their own subdirectory within the plugin path — never to their own `.claude` folder.",
      "priority": "high",
      "applies_when": "Continue the current task after compact.",
